	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;How should this be tested?&lt;br/&gt;
    1. Use org.apache.zeppelin.realm.LdapRealm as Shiro realm&lt;br/&gt;
    2. In the shiro_ini configruation, define a group search filter like this:&lt;br/&gt;
    ldapRealm.groupSearchFilter = (&amp;amp;(objectclass=groupofnames)(member=
{0}
&lt;p&gt;))&lt;br/&gt;
    or &lt;br/&gt;
    ldapRealm.groupSearchFilter = (&amp;amp;(objectclass=groupofnames)(cn=zeppelin-users*))&lt;br/&gt;
    3. Also define other LdapRealm parameters as necessary like rolesByGroup etc.&lt;br/&gt;
    4. When an LDAP user, who is part of the group that matches filter above, logs in, then the roles are applied. If the LDAP user is not part these defined groups, then the roles are not applied.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
